<article class="env-lemma" id="0329">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0329">Lemma <span data-tag="0329">10.160.7</span>.</a> Let $p > 0$ be a prime. Let $\Lambda $ be a Cohen ring with residue field of characteristic $p$. For every $n \geq 1$ the ring map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathbf{Z}/p^ n\mathbf{Z} \to \Lambda /p^ n\Lambda  \]
</div>
  <p> is formally smooth. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      If $n = 1$, this follows from Proposition <a href="/tag/0322" data-tag="0322">10.158.9</a>. For general $n$ we argue by induction on $n$. Namely, if $\mathbf{Z}/p^ n\mathbf{Z} \to \Lambda /p^ n\Lambda $ is formally smooth, then we can apply Lemma <a href="/tag/031L" data-tag="031L">10.138.12</a> to the ring map $\mathbf{Z}/p^{n + 1}\mathbf{Z} \to \Lambda /p^{n + 1}\Lambda $ and the ideal $I = (p^ n) \subset \mathbf{Z}/p^{n + 1}\mathbf{Z}$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>